================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY / ADAPTED CODE
================================================================================

The phase-based Visual Microphone processing in
`backend/processing/visual_microphone.py` and `backend/processing/signal_processing.py`
is adapted from:

  visual-mic-master  (bundled as visual-mic-master.zip)
  A Python re-implementation of MIT's "Visual Microphone".
  Copyright (c) 2020 Antonio Musolino and Davide Sforza
  Licensed under the MIT License (text identical to the above).

The algorithm itself is described in:

  A. Davis, M. Rubinstein, N. Wadhwa, G. J. Mysore, F. Durand, W. T. Freeman.
  "The Visual Microphone: Passive Recovery of Sound from Video."
  ACM Transactions on Graphics (Proc. SIGGRAPH) 33(4), 2014.

Complex steerable pyramids are computed with `pyrtools`
(Lab for Computational Vision, MIT License).

See README.md ("Attribution" and "What was adapted from visual-mic-master")
for a file-by-file breakdown of what was reused, changed, and newly written.
